==Old English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ang|non|þræll}} ({{cog|da|træl}}, {{cog|sv|träl}}), perhaps from Proto-Norse ''*þrāhilaʀ'', from {{der|ang|gem-pro|*þragilaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*þrahilaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*þrēhilaz}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*þreh-}}, {{m|gem-pro|*þreg-}}, {{m|gem-pro|*þrag-||to run}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*trāgʰ-||pull, drag, race, run}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|þrǣl}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=þrǣl|m}}

# a [[slave]], someone beholden to a [[lord]] or [[master]]

